  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "The line $ax + by + 1 = 0$ is perpendicular to $4x + 3y = 7$ and passes through $(9,7)$.\nFind the values of $a$ and $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=3,\\quad b=-4$.",
      "worked": "The original gradient is $-\\dfrac{4}{3}$, so the perpendicular gradient is $\\dfrac{3}{4}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\ny-7&=\\frac{3}{4}(x-9)\\\\\n4y-28&=3x-27\\\\\n3x-4y+1&=0.\n\\end{align*}$$\nComparing with $ax+by+1=0$ gives $a=3$ and $b=-4$. Check: $3(9)-4(7)+1=0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 56
  },
